# ── Old Python prototype files (removed from tracking, kept locally) ─────────
# These are the original Python PoC files — they live on disk but don't belong
# in the repository now that we have the Rust codebase.
chronos_agent.py
fhe_engine.py
posw.py
drand_client.py
benchmark.py
config.py
exceptions.py
interfaces.py
logger.py
memory_sanitizer.py
generate_pdf.py
# All root-anchored with a leading slash. Without it, these patterns match a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, which silently excluded standard Cargo
# layouts: `tests/` blocked `crates/*/tests/` (integration tests) and `security/`
# blocked `crates/*/src/security/`. Files already tracked were unaffected, so the
# breakage only showed up for newly added files — and showed up as CI passing
# because the test file was never committed.
/python/
/security/
/tests/
/test/
# `contracts/` was also ignored here as part of the legacy Python-era prototype.
# It is now first-class source (Groth16 verifier + attestation registry), so the
# entry is removed (already applied on main via #58). Solidity *build output*
# stays ignored above via `artifacts/` and `cache/`.
scripts/deploy.js
hardhat.config.js
chronos-bot/
chronos-rust/
codecov.yml
pyproject.toml
requirements.txt
release-please-config.json
docker-compose.yml
index.html
.nojekyll
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.release-please-manifest.json
package.json
package-lock.json

