# ── Scratch output from local build/test runs ─────────────────────────────────
# Debris from redirecting cargo output to files while debugging. Harmless, but it
# should never reach a commit. `*.log` is already ignored above via the LaTeX
# section; these cover the `.txt` equivalents.
#
# Root-anchored so it cannot swallow `.txt` fixtures inside `crates/`.
#
# `memory.txt` is deliberately included in this pattern: it is a local working
# copy of the paper text, kept on disk for reference. The paper itself is
# published, so committing a plain-text duplicate to the repo root would only add
# a second copy to keep in sync.
/*.txt
run*.log
s[0-9]*.log
t[0-9]*.log
bench-results.txt
test-results.txt

# ── Mission artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `ct_sk.bin` and `certN.bin` are named explicitly above; `*.bin` also covers
# `salt.bin` and the persisted `erasure_pk.bin` proving key, which is large and
# regenerable. Note that `mission_public.json` is deliberately NOT ignored — it
# holds only public commitments and is meant to be published alongside the paper.
/mission/
erasure_pk.bin
identity_pk.bin
operator.key

# ── Paper source, kept local ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The LaTeX source and its build output stay on disk and out of the repository.
# Remove this entry if the paper should be versioned alongside the artifact —
# `*.aux`, `*.log`, `*.out`, `*.toc` and `*.pdf` are already ignored above, so
# only the `.tex` would need tracking.
/paper/
